From 2166025fb2ee255c2d4d5a30ecdb247426cb3386 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:50:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 106/106] PS4: shader and pipeline work measured; the shader
 cache files kept whole

Pipelines built at boot from the game's shader cache and those built in play: Eden's translation
of their shaders to SPIR-V and the driver's creation timed, and RADV's pipeline cache hits read
(creation feedback, Vulkan 1.3). Uniform buffer copies sampled: how many repeat the slot's last.

The shader cache (vulkan.bin) was deleted whole when an entry failed to read or write (an append
cut short by a crash or a power cut): it is now cut back to the last whole entry. The driver's
pipeline cache (vulkan_pipelines.bin) is written beside the old one and renamed over it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01REmpC53sSK3VTcKMxWFSSb
